[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    538[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    539[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // Row 11 — negative size.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    540[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    541[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // The C computes the memcpy length as `cltq; shl $0x4`, i.e. it sign-extends
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    542[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // `int size` to 64 bits and multiplies by 16 with wraparound. For any negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    543[0m:[38;5;10m[49m // size that yields an enormous unsigned length and memcpy faults, so the call
